\begin_layout Standard
The time-domain model (reed_model, a Runge-Kutta 4 port of the MATLAB code RK4ode45cavity_reed_socket) projects the tongue on two uniform-cantilever modes and couples it to a closed cavity. It was updated in two steps, each replacing an assumption by a finite element result, and the coupled behaviour was then compared between three models.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The tongue first. The model accepts the modal parameters of the first mode reduced to the tip: modal mass 
\begin_inset Formula $m$
\end_inset
, modal stiffness 
\begin_inset Formula $k=m\omega_{1}^{2}$
\end_inset
, and the swept area 
\begin_inset Formula $\gamma=\int_{0}^{L}b(x)\phi(x)\,\mathrm{d}x$
\end_inset
